    pr_ref:  # da6d
    description: "**Defect.** The spec describes `nodes[].origin` as a scalar string in one place while framing it as a list elsewhere.\n\n**Evidence.** Spec §1775-1776 documents nodes[].origin as \"String, pass ID that created this node,\" while §259/§795 describe origin as a list supporting multi-pass attribution. The two descriptions of the same field contradict each other; the data model emits a list.\n\n**Contract.** The spec should describe `origin` with a single consistent type (list framing, matching the migrated data model).\n\n**Consequence.** A consumer reading the spec to learn the origin type encounters two incompatible descriptions; one following the scalar-string section writes parsing code that breaks on the list-typed field the map actually emits.\n\n**Related (not duplicate).** This is the docs-fix facet split out from the origin-list defect (INV-jidat tracks the data/producer side: list-typed but singleton). Editing the spec does not fix attribution; the producer fix does not fix the spec."  # da6d
    fields: {}  # da6d
